        {
          "sha": "015248f5eadb5ff12c881b85ccc1ba585966f27c",
          "author_name": "Brandon Fryslie",
          "author_email": "530235+brandon-fryslie@users.noreply.github.com",
          "timestamp": "2026-11-18T10:00:08-07:00",
          "message": "fix(storage): a storage folder's watch or stat fault clears when the OS answers again (tvhj)\n\nA refused or erroring watch, or a folder a judgment could not stat, no\nlonger ends its generation. The fault is derived from the handle's\ndeafness (taken at each window and at open, when the registry tells a\nmove of it) and the last judgment's stat, so the registry's period\nreopen and the next judgment clear it in place. A start or change of a\nfault is counted and logged once; a clear is logged. Only a folder that\ncould not be made stays terminal.\n"
        }
      ]
    },
